From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:27:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Perf and alloc unit tests: measure the work and wait for
 a state, not a count of rebuilds or the clock of a busy machine

sliceRecorder.perf.test.ts times a call as the smaller of its elapsed time and its CPU time, and divides each round by how much slower than its best this
process runs at that moment (a fixed loop timed in the same process), so a neighbour taking the core for a scheduler's quantum or slowing it down no longer
reads as a slow recorder; the limits are unchanged. detailStreaks.alloc.test.ts waits until the median of the last 11 windows is quiet (and again after the
collections) instead of for 1,200 or 4,000 rebuilds, says so when a case never settles, and has a test timeout that a busy machine does not run out of.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016zPE7K49ycKieo7wJdrBFN
