From 41381af82ce776b56f73c9815820b4b0ee78c543 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:32:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] e2e: wait for the state each failing spec was reading,
 not for a time; repeat a wall-clock measure

Reproduced under two workers and a busy loop: layers.spec.ts read the view before it had taken the landscape size (6.48 px a cell for 2.91; the canvas buffer was still
portrait 3 s after the resize), wind-detail-render.spec.ts ended its hand-over window of 4 s at 3 frames and a fade of 0.5, pace.spec.ts's tracker saw frames 2 to 4 s
apart and published nothing for two minutes (the spec now skips the drawing), and gallery-070.spec.ts saw the pause after 18 s against a bound of 30 s.
air-slice.spec.ts reads the layout only when the panel has drawn the scene's latest slice and its boxes have been the same for four frames (not reproduced).
wind-glyphs.spec.ts takes each slice-time measure up to four times from an empty log and keeps the best round.

